# AeroDash GitHub Issue Operations — Pre-Flight Rule

This rule ensures that whenever you interact with GitHub issues through the
GitHub MCP (search, create, update, comment), you first consult the local
project documentation so that every action is consistent with the repository's
conventions.

**This rule applies automatically to all agent interactions.** It is NOT
limited to the `/issue` command — it governs any situation where the agent
might create, update, search, or comment on a GitHub issue.

---

## 1. Mandatory Documentation Reads

Before calling ANY of the following GitHub MCP tools:

- `search_issues`
- `list_issues`
- `issue_write` (create or update)
- `issue_read`
- `add_issue_comment`

You MUST first read the following local files (unless you have already read
them earlier in the same conversation turn):

### 1.1 Issue Lifecycle & Labels

Read **`CONTRIBUTING.md`** (§8–§9) to obtain the current definitions for:

- **Issue Types:** Bug, Feature, Task (and their semantics)
- **Scope Labels:** `product`, `engineering`
- **Module Scopes:** `ac`, `ap`, `ad`, `fe`, `mb`, `pf`, `wx`, `ui`, `uq`,
  `sys`, `doc`, `sc`, `repo` (and any new scopes added since this rule was
  written)
- **Safety Tags:** `safety-critical`
- **Status Labels:** `open`, `accepted`, `ready`
- **Resolution Labels:** `fixed`, `duplicate`, `wont do`
- **Lifecycle Transitions:** which labels are added/removed at each stage

Do NOT assume these values from memory. The CONTRIBUTING.md file is the single
source of truth and may be updated at any time.

### 1.2 Issue Template Schemas

When creating a new issue, also read the relevant template from
`.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/`:

| Issue Type | Template File |
| :--- | :--- |
| Bug | `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug_report.yml` |
| Feature | `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/feature_request.yml` |
| Task | `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/sub_task.yml` |

Extract from the template:

- **Title prefix** (e.g., `[Bug]:`, `[Feat]:`, `[Task]:`)
- **Default labels** (e.g., `["Bug", "open"]`)
- **Required fields** and their validation rules
- **Optional fields** and their descriptions

### 1.3 Template Config

Read `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml` to confirm whether blank issues are
enabled and to see any configured contact links.

